-- Source module: Solutions.R6CxNetSim
/-!
# Chunk programs with phase frames (the physical simulation, any wire type)

A **chunk** at label `V` first moves some wires to `V` (each move `U → V` is one merged frame
change `edgeStepsM`, needing `EdgeOK V U`), then applies elementary scalar gates
`z_dst += c · z_src` (pointwise on the addresses) whose two wires are at `V`.

* `Inv lab Λ F`: the physical state `F` is the logical state `Λ` in the frames `Φ_{q_{lab w}}`.
* `chunk_sim` / `prog_sim`: a valid chunk (program) maps `Inv lab Λ F` to
  `Inv lab' (runOps ops Λ) (den · F)`.
* `prog_widths`: the child widths are the residual dimensions `Fd V U` of the moves.
-/

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false

